-- title:
--   1-ζ generates the maximal ideal of a DVR in ℚ(ζₚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, so that $L$ is generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $p$-th roots of unity; let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, equipped with an algebra structure over which $L$ is the fraction field of $A$, i.e. the structure map $A \to L$ identifies $L$ with the localisation of $A$ at its nonzero elements. Assume that the image of $p$ in $A$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A$ of $A$ (so the residue characteristic of $A$ is $p$), and let $z \in A$ be an element whose image in $L$ under the structure map is $\zeta$. The conclusion is that $\mathfrak{m}_A$ equals the ideal of $A$ generated by $1 - z$; equivalently, $1 - z$ is a uniformiser of $A$.
--
--   This is the standard fact that $p$ is totally ramified in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ with $1-\zeta$ a uniformiser at the unique prime above $p$, formulated for an arbitrary discrete valuation ring $A$ with fraction field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and which contains $\zeta$. It is used to obtain the factorisation of $p$ as a unit times the $(p-1)$-st power of a uniformiser in [`IsCyclotomicExtension.exists_isUnit_natCast_eq_mul_uniformizer_pow_sub_one`](thm.html#IsCyclotomicExtension.exists_isUnit_natCast_eq_mul_uniformizer_pow_sub_one), and thence in the analysis of charts on the modular curve $X_1(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDiscreteValuationRing_maximalIdeal_eq_span_one_sub_of_isPrimitiveRoot.lean

